        <div class="mt-16 bg-gray-900 text-white rounded-2xl p-8">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Decide on the drive before anything else. Rear-wheel drive belongs on any lawn that slopes or gets bagged, and front-wheel drive is fine on a flat lot full of turns. Then let your measured grass area, and how often the lawn outgrows you, settle gas versus battery. Once those calls are made, the Toro Recycler Personal Pace and the EGO LM2135SP suit most yards.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            After that, upkeep does the rest. A mid-range self-propelled mower with a tensioned drive cable, wheels kept free of packed clippings and a sharp blade can give most households close to ten years of easy mowing.
